    "topic": "Basic Query Builder",
    "question": "Laravel Query Builder kya hai aur Eloquent se kaise differ karta hai?",
    "explanation": "Query Builder DB facade ke through raw-ish, fluent SQL queries likhne deta hai bina Model class use kiye. Ye Eloquent se lightweight hota hai jab hume sirf data chahiye, model instance nahi.",
    "example": "Ek complex sales report banane ke liye jisme sirf aggregated numbers chahiye (SUM, COUNT), Query Builder use karna Eloquent models load karne se faster hota hai.",
    "code": "$totalSales = DB::table('orders')\n    ->where('status', 'completed')\n    ->sum('amount');\n\n$report = DB::table('orders')\n    ->select('status', DB::raw('COUNT(*) as total'))\n    ->groupBy('status')\n    ->get();",
    "codeExplanation": "DB::table() directly table par query build karta hai bina Eloquent model instantiate kiye, jo memory-efficient hai bulk aggregation ke liye.",
    "interviewAnswer": "The Query Builder provides a fluent interface for constructing SQL queries directly via the DB facade, without the overhead of Eloquent model hydration. It's ideal for performance-sensitive queries like reports or aggregations where full model objects aren't needed.",
    "tip": "Mention that Eloquent is actually built on top of Query Builder internally, so you always have access to it via Model::query()."
