    "question": "Service Container aur Facades ka basic concept kya hai?",
    "explanation": "Service Container Laravel ka dependency injection manager hai jo classes ko resolve aur instantiate karta hai. Facades static-like syntax dete hain in underlying services ko access karne ke liye (jaise Cache::get()).",
    "example": "Cache::remember() likhna asaan lagta hai, lekin ye actually Service Container se CacheManager instance resolve karke uska method call kar raha hota hai.",
    "code": "Cache::remember('products', 3600, function () {\n    return Product::all();\n});",
    "codeExplanation": "Cache facade behind the scenes cache manager ka instance container se resolve karta hai, aur remember() 1 hour tak result cache karke store karta hai.",
    "interviewAnswer": "The Service Container is Laravel's IoC (Inversion of Control) container responsible for managing class dependencies and performing dependency injection. Facades provide a convenient static interface to classes registered in the container, without sacrificing testability since they resolve real underlying instances.",
    "tip": "Common misconception: Facades don't mean 'static classes' - they're a syntax layer over container-resolved singletons, which keeps things testable via mocking."
