    "example": "Jab user /products URL hit karta hai, ye poora cycle chalta hai: index.php -> Kernel -> Middleware -> Router -> Controller -> View -> Response.",
    "code": "// public/index.php (simplified)\n$app = require_once __DIR__.'/../bootstrap/app.php';\n$kernel = $app->make(Kernel::class);\n$response = $kernel->handle($request = Request::capture());\n$response->send();",
    "codeExplanation": "Ye entry point request capture karta hai, HTTP Kernel ko handle karne deta hai (jo middleware aur routing chalata hai), aur final response ko send() karta hai browser ko.",
    "interviewAnswer": "Every request enters through public/index.php, which bootstraps the application and passes the request to the HTTP Kernel. The Kernel runs global and route middleware, the router matches the request to a controller action, and the resulting response travels back through the middleware before being sent to the client.",
    "tip": "This is a great question to demonstrate depth - mention Service Providers being booted during bootstrap as well."
