    "interviewAnswer": "Queues allow deferring time-consuming tasks - like sending emails, processing images, or generating reports - to be processed asynchronously in the background, rather than blocking the user's request. Laravel supports multiple queue drivers like database, Redis, and SQS, with worker processes consuming jobs from the queue.",
    "tip": "In production, mention using Supervisor to keep queue workers running continuously and restart them automatically if they crash."
