    "interviewAnswer": "Jobs encapsulate a single unit of work, like generating a report or processing an upload, in a dedicated class with a handle() method. Implementing ShouldQueue and calling dispatch() pushes the job onto a queue, where it's asynchronously processed by a worker without blocking the main application flow.",
    "tip": "Mention job retries and failed_jobs table - ->onQueue(), ->delay(), and $tries property control retry behavior for failed jobs."
